WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
For step two, look at the taller right-angled triangle, AFX. Its vertical side, AF, is simply

00:08.000 --> 00:14.240
the wheelbase L plus the front overhang K, and we just found the base FX in step one.

00:14.760 --> 00:21.020
Using Pythagoras' theorem a second time gives us the hypotenuse AX, the radius of the outer circle.

00:21.580 --> 00:27.280
And that leads immediately to step three. Since point G lies on that exact same circle,

00:27.280 --> 00:30.360
the distance GX is identical to AX.

